component GettingStarted() {
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-gray-50">
    <nav class="bg-teal-600 text-white py-6">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <a href="index.html" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Suko</a>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-sm font-medium text-teal-100">
          <a href="getting-started.html" class="text-white underline">Getting Started</a>
          <a href="language-reference.html" class="hover:text-white">Language Reference</a>
          <a href="components/index.html" class="hover:text-white">Components</a>
          <a href="roadmap.html" class="hover:text-white">Roadmap</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">Getting Started</h2>

      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">
        Comece rapidamente com o Suko em qualquer projeto Java/Kotlin.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-8 mb-8">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">1. Instalação</h3>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          O Suko está disponível como um CLI em jbang, que permite executar sem instalação:
        </p>
        <p class="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 p-6 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto mb-6 font-mono text-sm">
          jbang suko@suko-lang init my-project
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Ou instale via Gradle e use o plugin (o plugin Maven ainda não gera um descritor utilizável):
        </p>
        <p class="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 p-6 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto mb-6 font-mono text-sm">
          plugins &#123; id("io.suko.lang") version "0.1.0" &#125;
          suko &#123; sourceDir = file("src/main/suko") outputDir = file("build/generated-suko") &#125;
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-8 mb-8">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">2. Escreva o seu primeiro componente</h3>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Crie um ficheiro src/main/suko/components/Hello.sk:
        </p>
        <p class="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 p-6 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto mb-6 font-mono text-sm">
          package components;
          component Hello(String name) &#123;
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-teal-600">Olá, &#123;name&#125;!</div>
          &#125;
        </p>

        <p class="text-gray-700">
          O Suko compila isto para um template JTE que pode ser renderizado no seu application Java/Kotlin.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-8 mb-8">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">3. Renderize</h3>

        <p class="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 p-6 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto mb-6 font-mono text-sm">
          CodeResolver resolver = new DirectoryCodeResolver(Path.of("build/generated-suko"));
          TemplateEngine engine = TemplateEngine.create(resolver, ContentType.Html);
          TemplateOutput output = new StringOutput();
          engine.render("components/Hello.jte", Map.of("name", "Mundo"), output);
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-8">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Próximos passos</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
          <li>Leia a <a href="language-reference.html" class="text-teal-600">Language Reference</a></li>
          <li>Explore a <a href="components/index.html" class="text-teal-600">biblioteca de componentes</a></li>
          <li>Veja o <a href="roadmap.html" class="text-teal-600">roadmap do projeto</a></li>
          <li>Veja o <a href="https://github.com/DumiJDev/suko" class="text-teal-600">código-fonte completo</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="border-t border-gray-200 bg-white py-8">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 text-center text-gray-500 text-sm">
        <p>© 2026 Suko. Documentação gerada com Suko.</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </div>
}